quick-question (0.4.0-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release:
    - config replaces flat "profiles" with "gateways" that each list
      the "models" available on them; a gateway caps tool categories
      (read/write/exec), MCP servers and allow_danger, which a model
      may only narrow, never widen; selection is by [gateway/]model
      (-p), with ambiguous bare names refused
    - -y does every tool call without asking
    - -L writes a timestamped debug log of the whole exchange, with
      the command line as its first entry
    - a repeated tool call, including MCP calls, is answered from
      history instead of asking again or resending the search
    - the MCP gateway no longer runs qq's own tools, and "tools"/"mcp"
      are recognized
    - api_key_env now fails fast when it names an unset variable, and
      -l lists profiles
    - covers 0.3.0, which was not separately packaged

 -- Ian Lamont <imlamont@comcast.net>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

quick-question (0.2.0-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release:
    - local tools behind -r (read), -w (write and edit) and -x (run
      commands), each change confirmed on the terminal
    - approval prompts are refused after 120 seconds, so an unattended
      run cannot wait forever
    - example profile for a local Ollama server
    - OpenAI-compatible endpoints are the only supported kind

 -- Ian Lamont <imlamont@comcast.net>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 23:40:00 +0000

